    "source": "; BYTEFORGE // complete 8-bit CPU demonstration\n; R0/R1 are the Fibonacci pair. R2 is the loop counter.\n; 8-bit arithmetic wraps at 0xFF and updates Z/N/C/V flags.\n; CALL/RET exercises the byte stack; STORE8/LOAD8 exercise RAM.\nCONST R0 0\nCONST R1 1\nCONST R2 12\nCONST R3 0\nCALL FIBONACCI\nHALT\n\nFIBONACCI:\nOUT8 0 R0\nSTORE8 R3 R0\nINC8 R3\nADD8 R4 R0 R1\nMOV8 R0 R1\nMOV8 R1 R4\nDEC8 R2\nJNZ8 FIBONACCI\nLOAD8 R5 0x20\nRET\n"
